comments[9]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-29T08:28:14.112Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: complete all-status corpus, live open and in_progress lists, request-specific search and full pm-89297t data show the serial allocation repair is already closed and shipped. This new leaf owns the repeated compound-test timeout on current native evidence, not the completed allocation or the distinct raw-rename fixture defect."
  "2026-10-29T08:29:47.767Z","harness:codex","Split the compound native test into unstaged refusal, four independently named invalid-index variants, rollback preservation, and junction settlement. Each retains real Git setup and the unchanged 30000ms deadline; every original assertion remains and each invalid variant now also verifies staged-settlement refusal without history mutation. This increases case attribution without changing serial partitioning or job limits."
  "2026-10-29T08:30:33.667Z","harness:codex","The original native failure remains run40837931196/job123327040143: the same indexed-proof case failed both attempts at30000ms. Closed pm-89297t already moved this file into the serial phase; that shipped fix remains intact. Current work separates independently observable refusal and preservation contracts and requires a complete native rerun for acceptance."
  "2026-10-29T08:32:42.380Z","harness:codex","Focused source run passes all22 real-Git LF/CRLF cases after separating independent contracts, alongside lock and packed Node/Bun continuation tests. Full selected cohort:9files195tests pass. Native Windows proof remains pending; the old timeout is retained as failed evidence."
  "2026-10-29T10:05:12.783Z","harness:codex","CodeRabbit review 5695929096 identified that splitting rollback and junction scenarios lost same-fixture receipt re-authentication after rollback. Restore byte-for-byte receipt preservation and restaging/authentication assertions inside the rollback scenario, retaining the independent junction contract and unchanged 30-second deadlines."
  "2026-10-29T10:25:02.884Z","harness:codex","Restored same-fixture rollback acceptance: preserve receipt bytes, re-stage the identical receipt, authenticate its durable ID, successfully settle it, and retain unrelated staged work. All 22 LF/CRLF real-Git cases pass within unchanged per-test limits as part of the 166-test final review-fix cohort. The isolated junction scenario remains intact."
  "2026-10-29T10:35:42.176Z","harness:codex","Native Windows proof before the final review assertions: run 40849657299 at 943470bca, shard 1/4 job 123368461427 passed 2695 tests across 221 files with 106 platform skips. The separated portability file passed all 22 LF/CRLF cases, preserving each 30-second deadline. The later 7aef94d8a same-fixture rollback assertions pass locally and await the new exact-head matrix."
  "2026-10-29T13:24:00.403Z","harness:codex","Current native Windows shard3 at source 1a242f11f fails the separate merge-receipt-settlement keeper twice at its unchanged 30000ms deadline (run40864851705/job123416907459). All 3122 other tests pass, including the 78-test CLI JSON cohort. Full live predecessor reads confirm the serial allocation and authoritative receipt fixes remain completed. Reuse this active native-receipt proof leaf to separate independent attribution, invalid-audit, corrupt-history and legacy-recovery contracts while preserving real worktrees, every assertion, same-fixture retry/idempotence, serial allocation and deadlines."
  "2026-10-29T13:33:00.274Z","harness:codex","Both linked native-receipt commands pass on the revised test tree: 22 indexed-proof cases and four independent worktree-settlement cases. An AST assertion inventory retains all 41 original settlement assertions; each case owns isolated real worktrees, and the first keeps interrupted persistence, retry, commit and stale-copy idempotence together. Typecheck, ESLint, docstrings and duplicate detection pass. Current-source Windows shard1 run40864851705/job123416907376 passes all2695 applicable tests, including all22 portability cases and17 lease-fencing cases, with no unhandled errors. The shard3 JSON cohort passes but its original compound settlement test times out twice; the revised four-case native acceptance remains pending."
